# vehje-lower. backlog

Designed but deferred. Names stay unbackticked until they ship.

## The dev-time equality-saturation e-graph

The heavier lowering stratum: a no-alloc bounded streaming equality-saturation
over a slotted and colored e-graph, run ahead of time for bundled scripts where
the e-graph can take its time. It unifies constant folding, macro expansion,
CSE, and the algebraic identities into one saturate-then-extract, and it grows a
measured linear (not exponential) size because hashcons congruence deduplicates
equivalent forms, with the bounded streaming window as a hard termination and
memory safety mechanism. This is the flagged original research; it lands behind
the same `Lower` fold interface as the cheap subset (the reserved `Saturate`
strategy variant), so its arrival is additive. The extractor is a bottom-up cost
fixpoint bound to the iterative work-stack discipline, never recursive, because
recursion is a hard compiler wall, and the cost function must be effect-and-
machine-aware rather than pure rewrite-count (equality saturation alone can pick
a form that is cheaper by rewrite count but worse on the machine).

## Deepdive owed

A deepdive on the three-way lowering seam (the cheap subset, the dev-time
e-graph, and why lowering is a distinct operation from checking and emission)
lands with the saturation stratum.
